// Debug sessions (api_minor 14; features "debugger", "debugger-live";
// docs/debugger.md). One session model whatever runs the code: revkit's
// p-code emulator, a live process or board behind a GDB remote stub
// (gdbserver, QEMU, OpenOCD, J-Link), a process the daemon launches, or a
// saved trace replayed, or a crash dump (an ELF core file, a Windows
// minidump; api_minor 102). Every stop is recorded on the session's timeline,
// which the state, register and memory calls can read at any snapshot.
//
// Like EmulatorService, a session is the caller's state, not a fact about
// the binary: nothing is asserted, no revision is made. Live targets run
// code on the daemon's host or reach other machines, so they are off unless
// the daemon was started with --debug-live (feature "debugger-live").
